  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA XBR-65X900F (2018, BRAVIA_ATV3_4K, MediaTek MT5891), US/Canada firmware\nProduct BRAVIA_ATV3_4K_UC, model string \"BRAVIA 4K GB ATV3\". Android TV 9 (API 28), 2 GB RAM.\nFirmware BRAVIA_ATV3_4K_UC-user 9 PTT1.190515.001.S54 672201 release-keys, security patch 2022-01-05\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-xbr-65x900f/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-xbr-65x900f/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nApplied 2026-10-19 and checked across a reboot (list still disabled, launcher still Home, HDMI and\nLive TV fine). Not lived with for weeks yet: re-enable anything that breaks with `pm enable <package>`.\n\nSame Android 9 firmware build as examples/sony-xbr-x900e and sony-bravia-4k-gb (ATV2), one platform\ngeneration newer (ATV3, MT5891). Package set is the same apart from the ATV3 panel/HDMI services.\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (restore.sh's default).\nLive TV / input app: com.sony.dtv.tvx. Keep it: it also plays every HDMI input and the ATSC tuner.\nKeep: com.sony.dtv.tvinput.*, braviasync* (HDMI-CEC), remotepairing, rcpowerkey, uinputservice,\nimeproxy, sonysystemservice, settingsprovider, all com.mediatek.* and mtktvapi.agent, timers.\nAlready off on this TV before the list (owner or factory): tv.samba.ssm and com.sony.dtv.promos (both\nlisted below anyway), com.sony.rvu, actionmenu.plugin.harmony, Vudu, Play Movies, Play Games.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- ADB: Developer options > USB debugging opens port 5555 (Android 9: no Wireless debugging pairing);\nthe TV then shows the usual \"Allow USB debugging?\" prompt. Tick \"Always allow\".\n- The sponsored banner at the top of the stock home (Hulu, Apple TV+ promos) comes from\ncom.google.android.tvlauncher itself and survives disabling tvrecommendations; only replacing the\nlauncher removes it.\n- Sony Settings pages (About, Status) return an empty screencap; read them with `uiautomator dump`.\n- The retail model number is not in getprop or UPnP (both say \"BRAVIA 4K GB ATV3\"); read it off the\nsticker or the Help app.\n- Launcher works. Same as the X900E: the stock launcher's HOME filter wins until\ncom.google.android.tvlauncher is disabled; disable it, then `cmd package set-home-activity\ncom.gathin.tvhome/.MainActivity`. Home key from inside apps returns to the new launcher.\n- Inputs works: HDMI 1-4 (HDMI 3/ARC), Video and Live TV listed via com.sony.dtv.tvx. This firmware\nreports real per-port status (\"No device\" / \"Connected\"), not every port as connected.\nconfig.xml: hidden_apps com.sony.dtv.tvx and com.sony.dtv.tvxlauncher.programguide,\nlive_tv_package com.sony.dtv.tvx.\nACR viewing tracker",
